# Cloud manual testing (Cloud Studio zsh/bash)

**Canonical order**: [CLOUD_VALIDATION.md](../docs/architecture/CLOUD_VALIDATION.md) (Phase A–G). This file is the **copy-paste cheat sheet** for assistants and operators.

## Shell convention

- **Tencent Cloud Studio GPU** default terminal is **zsh** (`➜` prompt). Assistant-facing commands use **bash/zsh** syntax.
- **Do not** paste PowerShell (`$VAR = "..."`, `Invoke-WebRequest`, `Join-Path`) into Cloud Studio zsh — causes `command not found: =`.
- **Windows local** (PowerShell): same logical steps; translate paths (`D:\...` vs `/workspace/DocuVision`).
- Optional: run `pwsh` in Cloud Studio only when the user explicitly wants PowerShell.

## One-time setup

```bash
export REPO_ROOT="/workspace/DocuVision"
cd "$REPO_ROOT"
git pull   # or your feature branch

# Pro GPU venv (separate from Lite)
python3 -m venv ~/docuvision_env
source ~/docuvision_env/bin/activate
cd "$REPO_ROOT/backend"
./install_pro_gpu.sh   # or per requirements.txt header
cp -n .env.cloud .env  # do not commit .env
```

Lite CPU validation uses **`docuvision_lite_env`** — see `apps/lite/backend/tests/README.md`. **Never mix** Pro and Lite venvs.

